From 5d0b7921cfbef2fb4b2b36021a03dccefdaf1302 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: review <review@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:39:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Assert that the split adds no allocation to ClimaCore's
 solve, and revert the copied loop

On Julia 1.10 the coupled solve that both paths run allocates 1056 bytes
per call, so the unsplit and the split solve allocate the same, and the
copied stationary iteration changed nothing measurable. It goes back to
ClimaCore's run_field_matrix_solver!. The test now asserts that the split
allocates no more than the unsplit solve, and keeps the zero assertion as
known broken on Julia 1.10 with the measured value in a comment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LA3FukgbRCMkra999BhdDw
